# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAID arena 1
#
# Read by src/game/RaidLevel.cpp at room load, and again on F7 without leaving
# the room. Written by tools/raid_editor.html, and perfectly hand-editable.
#
# Units are the game's own. X and Z are the floor plane; Y is NEGATIVE UPWARDS,
# so a ceiling is a negative number. Every coordinate is read back UNSIGNED by
# the collision and camera-zone tests, so keep the whole level at positive X/Z
# below 32768.
#
#   ambient <r> <g> <b>                          12-bit channels, 0..4095
#   light   <x> <y> <z> <r> <g> <b> <radius>     up to 8; radius 0 is a BLACK light
#   cam     <fx> <fy> <fz> <tx> <ty> <tz> <fov>  fov is a focal length, not an angle
#   camzone <cam> <x0> <z0> <x1> <z1>            walk in here, switch to that camera
#   spawn   <x> <z> <angle>                      0 = +X, 0x400 = +Z, 4096 = a turn
#   box     <x0> <y0> <z0> <x1> <y1> <z1> <flags> <shade> <r> <g> <b>
#   enemy   <x> <z> <angle> <type>
#
# box flags: 1 draw, 2 collide, 4 checkerboard.   shade is in hundredths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ver 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The guardhouse bathroom (Stage 4, ROOM4070), MODELLED in 3D after its two
# backgrounds (RC4070 / RC4071). The previous arena is raid1_arena.lvl.
#
# Everything here is MEASURED off those pictures: rays cast through the
# room's own two cameras (the RDT's camera records, which project the
# pictures to the pixel) onto the floor, the walls and the rims' planes. The
# walls stand on the room's collision records (RDT +0x4C), which agree.
#
# Materials (tbox / mesh tex ids):
#   cut out of the pictures by tools/build_raid_textures.py (not tracked):
#     t1 wall boards  t2 floor tiles  t3 enamel  t4 dark wood  t5 the door
#     t6 the rack's towel  t10 the bath mat  t15 the mat by the pan
#     t16 green plaster  t17 skirting  t18 the bath's outside  t19 the
#     cistern  t20 the pan's lid  t21 the bath towel
#     t26 the cistern's sides  t27 the rail's cap
#   painted by tools/build_raid_materials.py (tracked):
#     t7 brass  t9 towel cloth  t11 porcelain  t13 iron  t14 soap  t23 nickel
#     t24 the bottle  t28 amber glass
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

ambient 600 580 620

# The light, over the mat and the bath where the pictures have their pool of
# it; a second over the basin corner, which the pictures show lit too; and a
# dim fill for the bounce.
light 3900 -3000 8300 255 226 180 8500
light 7300 -2400 9600  80  84  96 6500
light 6900 -3100 6600 200 190 170 6500
light 5200 -3000  4100  90 104 150 6500    # room 003's corridor
light 12000 -3200 7000 110 128 190 9500    # its bedroom

# The room's own camera 0, high over the door.
cam  4914 -7812  9936   5094  -936  7866  230
# Room 003 next door (ROOM4060, its own cameras 1 and 4, moved with the room -
# see "Room 003" below): down its corridor, and over its bedroom.
cam  6554  -558  3984   1748 -1908  4254  230
cam 13448 -3636  9726  10766 -1116  4866  230

camzone 0   1872  5454   8298 10818     # the bathroom
camzone 1   1730  3012   9290  5154     # room 003's corridor
camzone 2   9290  3012  14528 11562     # room 003's bedroom

spawn 6000 8000 2048

# Floor and ceiling (a plate above the floor is seen from below only).
tbox  1872         0  5454   8298         0 10818  65 2 1543 100
tbox  1572 -4000  5154   8598 -4000 11118   1 1 1600 35

# Walls: boards, on the collision records' inner faces.
tbox  1572 -4000  5154   1872         0 11118   1 1 1600 100   # low X
# high X (basin side), cut round the mirror's glass (flag 64: the four pieces
# take their boards from the world origin, so they still line up)
tbox  8298 -4000  5154   8598         0  6140  65 1 1600 100
tbox  8298 -4000  6980   8598         0 11118  65 1 1600 100
tbox  8298 -4000  6140   8598 -3130  6980  65 1 1600 100
tbox  8298 -2080  6140   8598         0  6980  65 1 1600 100
tbox  1872 -4000  5154   2407         0  5454  65 1 1600 100   # far, round the doorway
tbox  3807 -4000  5154   8298         0  5454  65 1 1600 100
tbox  2407 -4000  5154   3807 -3195  5454  65 1 1600 100
tbox  1872 -4000 10728   3690         0 11028   65 1 1600 100   # near, bath side - one plane with the pan side (the collision
#   record is 90 deeper here; drawn at 10818 it showed a step up the wall)
tbox  3690 -4000 10728   8298         0 11118   65 1 1600 100   # near, pan side

